  "reason": "Evidence: config_003 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) achieved the best accuracy (0.7250), and the RNA encoder (scvi_n200 vs scgpt) is clearly the dominant factor (~0.21 gap). Fusion method (weighted vs concat) shows only a marginal difference (0.7250 vs 0.7207). The image encoder dimension remains unexplored for the top-performing RNA encoder. Question: Does resnet50 match or exceed imagenet_vit_l when paired with scvi_n200, transformer, and weighted fusion? This is a clean single-variable change from the best config. Why this is the best use of experiment 6: It reduces uncertainty on the second-most-important design axis (image encoder) while keeping all proven settings fixed. If resnet50 performs comparably, it confirms the current config is near-optimal and we can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning; if it underperforms significantly, it validates imagenet_vit_l and narrows the search space for experiments 7-10."
